lines:
Your mind's wisdom measures all that can be known;
your speech of fine explanation adorns the ears of the fortunate;
your body is radiant with the glory of renown:
I bow to you, meaningful to see, hear and remember.

Chenrezig, great treasure of compassion beyond concepts;
Manjushri, lord of stainless wisdom;
Lord of Secrets, who destroys every demonic force;
Tsongkhapa, crown jewel of the scholars of the Land of Snows:
at the feet of Lobsang Drakpa I make my request.

Freedom and fortune are hard to find, and life does not last;
by training your mind in this, stop clinging to this life.
Karma never fails, and samsara is suffering;
thinking of this again and again, stop clinging to future lives.

With skill and compassion you were born in the Shakya clan;
you defeated the forces of Mara that no one else could overcome;
your body shines like a mountain of gold:
King of the Shakyas, I bow to you.

King of Lamps, Steadfast and Powerful, Whose Vision Fulfils All Aims;
Glorious Ornament of Love; Sacred Glory Renowned for Virtue;
Renowned for Vast Vision Toward All;
Glorious, Powerful and Renowned, Lofty as Mount Meru;
Glory Renowned for Seeing All Beings;
Glory of Supreme Power and Fame, Who Brings Contentment:
by hearing even your names auspicious glory grows.
To the eight sugatas I bow.

Your wisdom, deeds and skill are beyond imagining;
you have a samadhi as indestructible as a vajra;
embodiment of effortless compassion, protector of the world:
I pray at the feet of Tekchok Dorje.

Hearing scripture and reasoning frees us from the veil of not knowing;
reflecting on the instructions overcomes the darkness of doubt;
the light born of meditation shows things exactly as they are:
may the light of these three kinds of wisdom grow.

The meaning of the ground is the two truths, free of the extremes of permanence and nothingness;
the supreme path is the two accumulations, free of the extremes of exaggeration and denial;
the fruit attained is the two benefits, free of the extremes of samsara and peace:
may we meet this Dharma that is free of error.

The ground to purify is mind itself, the union of clarity and emptiness;
the means of purification is the great vajra yoga of Mahamudra;
what is purified is the passing stains of confusion:
may the fruit of purification, the stainless dharmakaya, become manifest.

Confidence in the view is cutting through misconceptions about the ground;
the key to meditation is keeping to that without distraction;
the best conduct is training in all aspects of meditation:
may we have confidence in view, meditation and conduct.

All phenomena are the display of mind;
mind is no mind, empty of any essence of mind;
empty and unceasing, it appears as anything at all:
examining well, may we cut through to its root.

Our own appearances, which never existed, we mistake for objects;
through ignorance we mistake our own awareness for a self;
through grasping at two we wander in the expanse of existence:
may we cut through ignorance and confusion at the root.

Appearance is mind, and emptiness too is mind;
realization is mind, and confusion is our own mind;
arising is mind, and ceasing too is mind:
may all misconceptions be cut through within the mind.

Free of mental fabrication, this is Mahamudra;
free of extremes, it is the Great Middle Way;
because it includes everything, it is also called Dzogchen:
may we gain the confidence that knowing one realizes the meaning of all.

Great bliss without attachment, unbroken;
clear light without grasping at characteristics, free of veils;
non-thought beyond the intellect, spontaneously present:
may these effortless experiences continue without a break.

Grasping at good experiences is freed by itself;
the confusion of bad thoughts is naturally pure in the expanse;
ordinary mind has nothing to reject or accept, lose or gain:
may we realize the truth of reality, beyond elaboration.

May we strive in practice and may the sacred Dharma grow;
may we always practise you and see your supreme face;
and may precious bodhicitta that realizes emptiness
grow and increase like the waxing moon.

May the lives of the holders of the teaching be stable, their deeds and wishes fulfilled;
may the Sangha communities flourish and grow together;
may adverse conditions be pacified and all we wish for be accomplished:
may the Sakya teaching blaze!
